[{"_1":2},"routes/docs-slug",{"_3":4},"data",{"_5":6,"_7":8},"content","# World Graph\n\nThe World Graph is a visual representation of your story's lore. It turns abstract notes into a tangible, navigable network of characters, locations, and artifacts.\n\n## Visualizing Connections\nStorytelling is about relationships. The World Graph highlights:\n- **Character Networks**: Who knows whom? Who is related?\n- **Spatial Mapping**: How are locations connected?\n- **Artifact Ownership**: Where is the \"Ancient Key\" currently located in your world?\n\n## Graph Intelligence\nThe graph is more than just a pretty picture:\n- **Dynamic Updates**: As you add details to your characters in the Series Bible, the graph updates automatically.\n- **AI Synthesis**: Use the graph to ask the AI to identify \"influence clusters\"—characters who appear most frequently in key arcs.\n- **Lore Discovery**: Find \"orphaned\" entities (lore items you created but never actually used in your manuscript).\n\n## Pro Tip\nUse the **Context Lens** to filter the graph by a specific Arc. This will hide everything irrelevant to that specific plot thread, allowing you to focus on the relationships that matter for the scene you are currently writing.\n","slug","graph"]
